questions.question_text:
A rectangle is cut along the dashed diagonal.
What pieces are produced?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.5,0);
\coordinate (C) at (4.5,2.5);
\coordinate (D) at (0,2.5);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (A)--(C);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

A parallelogram is cut along the dashed line.
Where should the left triangle be moved to make a rectangle?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (4.7,0);
\coordinate (C) at (6.1,2.6);
\coordinate (D) at (1.4,2.6);
\draw (A)--(B)--(C)--(D)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (D)--(1.4,0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
